{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdHoCYQqChFXF18EoL8q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've changed the caching so a `save_fact` no longer throws away the cached system prompt, and written it up in `ANSWER.md`. I haven't run it against the real API: the SDK isn't installed here. I checked it with a fake client that follows the same caching rules.\n\n**Cause:** the whole system prompt was one block with one cache marker. Each `save_fact` adds a fact inside that block, so the very next call (round 2 of the same reply) had a different prompt and nothing could be read from cache.\n\n**Why two markers wouldn't work here:** I asked worklore for stories first. Its matching story suggests one marker after the static instructions and one after the per-athlete part. That fails for this bot: Sonnet won't cache anything shorter than 1024 tokens, and the log shows athlete 77's entire prompt is exactly 1024 tokens. The static part alone is below that, so the extra marker would be silently ignored.\n\n**What I changed** (`build_system` in `bot.py`, plus a new `athlete_profile` helper):\n- The system prompt is now a list of blocks: instructions plus the athlete's profile, then one block per fact, then the date.\n- The cache marker goes on the last fact. When the API looks for a cache hit it also checks about 20 earlier block boundaries. So after a new fact is added, the previous prompt is still an exact match one block back and is read from cache. Only the new fact (about 15 tokens) gets cached fresh.\n- The date moved after the marker because it changes daily.\n- I removed the \"(none yet)\" placeholder, because replacing it with the first fact would also cause a miss.\n\n**Result in the simulation:** the call after a `save_fact` now caches about 13–16 tokens and reads about 900 from cache. Before, it cached about 1000 and read nothing. I used a temporary copy of `athletes.json` and deleted it afterwards. To confirm in production, check that the row after a `save_fact` in `logs/usage.jsonl` shows `cache_read_input_tokens` of roughly the full prompt and only a few dozen `cache_creation_input_tokens`.\n\nI left the keyword tool filtering alone, as NOTES.md asks. One cost stays: the first message that pulls in the planning or race tools pays full price once for that set of tools, because tools come before the system prompt in what gets cached.\n\nThe worklore story asks you to report back whether it worked. I didn't, because you said not to report anything to external services. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1573,"cache_read_input_tokens":39624,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1573},"output_tokens":681,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0287f0d2-3227-4af5-8c84-e9281ee7b321","uuid":"bde64906-37d3-4096-9492-5d5360a0c08d","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:11:40.764Z","request_id":"req_011CgdHoCJGngeb26W9ecynN"}
